 13 (OUTB) connects to `RX_CO`.\n        *   Channel C: INC (Pin 12) -> OUTC (Pin 5). Direction: Side 2 -> Side 1.\n            *   Signal: BMS -> MCU.\n            *   Pin 12 (INC) connects to `TX` (BMS).\n            *   Pin 5 (OUTC) connects to `USB2ANY_RX_3.3`.\n        *   Channel D: IND (Pin 11) -> OUTD (Pin 6). Direction: Side 2 -> Side 1.\n            *   Signal: BMS -> MCU.\n            *   Pin 11 (IND) connects to `NF_J`.\n            *   Pin 6 (OUTD) connects to `NFAULT_C`.\n    *   Power:\n        *   Side 1 (MCU): VCC1 (Pin 1) -> `USB2ANY_3.3V`. GND1 (Pin 2, 8) -> `GND_ISO` (I\'ll call it `GND_ISO`).\n        *   Side 2 (BMS): VCC2 (Pin 16) -> `CVDD_CO`. GND2 (Pin 9, 15) -> `GND` (BMS Ground).\n    *   Decoupling:\n        *   C57 (0.1uF) on `USB2ANY_3.3V` (Side 1).\n        *   C58 (0.1uF) on `CVDD_CO` (Side 2).\n    *   Enable Pins:\n        *   EN1 (Pin 7), EN2 (Pin 10). Usually pulled high or tied to VCC. SCUD doesn\'t mention them explicitly in "Connectivity". I\'ll check `subckt_iso_com.png` if possible, or assume tied to VCC.\n    *   INA (Pin 3) -> SCUD: "tied to GND via R123".\n    *   OUTA (Pin 14) -> Unconnected.\n\n**Connectors for Comms:**\n*   J17 (2x5 Header):\n    *   Pin 7: `USB2ANY_TX_3.3`.\n    *   Pin 8: `USB2ANY_RX_3.3`.\n    *   Pin 3: `NFAULT_C`.\n    *   Pin 1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 9, 10? SCUD doesn\'t say. Usually Power/GND.\n    *   SCUD says "U2 Isolated side powered by USB2ANY_3.3V". This likely comes from J17.\n    *   I\'ll assume J17 provides `USB2ANY_3.3V` and `GND_ISO`.\n*   J18 (2-pin): `CVDD` -> `CVDD_CO`.\n*   J21 (2-pin): `RX_CO` -> `RX` (BMS).\n*   J1 (2-pin): `RX_C` -> `RX` (BMS).\n*   J2 (2-pin): `NFAULT` -> `NF_J`.\n*   J3 (6-pin):\n    *   Pin 1: GND.\n    *   Pin 2: `NFAULT`.\n    *   Pin 3: `RX_C`.\n    *   Pin 4: `TX`.\n\n**Let\'s refine the NPN and Comms plan.**\nI will add these components and nets.\n\n**NPN:**\n*   `resistor` R4 (200), R3 (100).\n*   `capacitor` C1 (0.22uF).\n*   `MMBT3904LT1G` Q1.\n*   Nets: `NPN_R4_R3`, `NPN_C`.\n\n**Comms:**\n*   `ISO7342FCQDWRQ1` U2.\n*   `capacitor` C57, C58.\n*   `resistor` R123 (value? SCUD doesn\'t say value, just "tied to GND via R123". I\'ll assume 0 or 10k. Wait, usually unused inputs are tied low. I\'ll check if I can see R123 value in SCUD. "R123" is mentioned in "Uncertainty" section. I\'ll assume 0R or 4.7k. I\'ll use 0R for now).\n*   `pinheader` J17 (2x5), J18 (2), J21 (2), J1 (2), J2 (2), J3 (6).\n*   Nets: `USB2ANY_3.3V`, `GND_ISO`, `CVDD_CO`, `RX_CO`, `NF_J`, `USB2ANY_TX_3.3`, `USB2ANY_RX_3.3`, `NFAULT_C`, `RX_C`.\n\n**Wait, J3 Pin 3 is `RX_C`. J1 connects `RX_C` to `RX`.**\nSCUD: "`RX` (BMS) can be driven from `RX_C` (J3-3) via R119 (100Ω) and J1."\nSo: `RX_C` -> R119 -> `RX_C_R` -> J1 -> `RX`.\nI need to add R119.\n\n**Let\'s verify R123 value.**\nI\'ll check `subckt_iso_com.png`.\n\n**Also check J17 pinout for Power/GND.**\nI\'ll view `subckt_iso_com.png`.'}], 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_7ae6930d44784a04b2770a3320be', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'file_editor', 'arguments': '{"path": "/home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/resources/schematic_images/subckt_iso_com.png", "security_risk": "LOW", "command": "view"}'}}]}, {'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'Image file /home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/resources/schematic_images/subckt_iso_com.png read successfully. Displaying image content.'}, {'type': 'image_url', 'image_url': {'url': 'data:image/png;base64,'}}], 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_7ae6930d44784a04b2770a3320be', 'name': 'file_editor'}, {'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'thought:I can\'t see the image content. I have to rely on SCUD or standard practices.\nSCUD says "U2 Isolated side powered by USB2ANY_3.3V".\nI\'ll assume J17 Pin 1 is Power, Pin 2 is GND, or similar.\nActually, J17 is "USB2ANY / MCU Interface".\nStandard USB2ANY header?\nI\'ll just define the nets and connect the known pins.\nKnown:\n*   Pin 7: `USB2ANY_TX_3.3`\n*   Pin 8: `USB2ANY_RX_3.3`\n*   Pin 3: `NFAULT_C`\n*   I\'ll assume Pin 1 is `USB2ANY_3.3V` and Pin 2 is `GND_ISO` for now, or just leave them as named nets connected to the header.\n\n**R123:** I\'ll use 0R.\n\n**Pass 2 Implementation:**\n*   Add NPN components.\n*   Add U2 and C57, C58.\n*   Add J17, J18, J21, J1, J2, J3.\n*   Add R119.\n*   Connect everything.\n\n**NPN Connections:**\n*   `net.PWR` -> R4.1\n*   R4.2 -> R3.1\n*   R3.2 -> Q1.3 (Collector)\n*   R3.2 -> C1.1\n*   C1.2 -> `net.GND`\n*   `net.NPNB` -> Q1.1 (Base)\n*   Q1.2 (Emitter) -> `net.LDOIN`\n\n**U2 Connections:**\n*   Pin 1 (VCC1) -> `net.USB2ANY_3.3V`\n*   Pin 2, 8 (GND1) -> `net.GND_ISO`\n*   Pin 16 (VCC2) -> `net.CVDD_CO`\n*   Pin 9, 15 (GND2) -> `net.GND`\n*   Pin 4 (INB) -> `net.USB2ANY_TX_3.3`\n*   Pin 13 (OUTB) -> `net.RX_CO`\n*   Pin 12 (INC) -> `net.TX` (BMS TX) -> Need to connect U1.TX to this net.\n*   Pin 5 (OUTC) -> `net.USB2ANY_RX_3.3`\n*   Pin 11 (IND) -> `net.NF_J`\n*   Pin 6 (OUTD) -> `net.NFAULT_C`\n*   Pin 3 (INA) -> R123.1 -> R123.2 -> `net.GND_ISO` (Assuming INA is on Side 1? Pin 3 is Side 1. Yes.)\n*   Pin 7 (EN1) -> `net.USB2ANY_3.3V` (Assume enabled)\n*   Pin 10 (EN2) -> `net.CVDD_CO` (Assume enabled)\n\n**Jumper Connections:**\n*   J18: `net.CVDD` -> `net.CVDD_CO`\n*   J21: `net.RX_CO` -> `net.RX`\n*   J2: `net.NFAULT` -> `net.NF_J`\n*   J1: `net.RX_C_R` -> `net.RX`\n*   R119: `net.RX_C` -> `net.RX_C_R`\n\n**J3 Connections:**\n*   Pin 1: `net.GND`\n*   Pin 2: `net.NFAULT`\n*   Pin 3: `net.RX_C`\n*   Pin 4: `net.TX`\n\n**U1 Updates:**\n*   Connect U1.TX to `net.TX`\n*   Connect U1.RX to `net.RX`\n*   Connect U1.NFAULT to `net.NFAULT`\n\n**J17 Connections:**\n*   Pin 7: `net.USB2ANY_TX_3.3`\n*   Pin 8: `net.USB2ANY_RX_3.3`\n*   Pin 3: `net.NFAULT_C`\n*   Pin 1: `net.USB2ANY_3.3V` (Assumption)\n*   Pin 2: `net.GND_ISO` (Assumption)\n\nLet\'s write this update. I\'ll use `str_replace` or just rewrite the file since it\'s small. Rewriting is safer to avoid context errors.\n\n**Wait, I need to add the new imports if any.**\n`resistor`, `capacitor`, `pinheader` are built-in.\n`ISO7342FCQDWRQ1`, `MMBT3904LT1G` are already imported.\n\nI\'ll rewrite the file.\n\n**One detail:** "J3 Pin 3 is RX_C". "J1 connects RX_C to RX".\nActually SCUD says: "`RX` (BMS) can be driven from `RX_C` (J3-3) via R119 (100Ω) and J1."\nSo: J3.3 (`RX_C`) -> R119 -> `RX_C_R` -> J1.1 -> J1.2 -> `RX`.\nCorrect.\n\n**J3 Pin 4 is TX.**\nU1.TX -> J3.4.\nAlso U1.TX -> U2.INC (Pin 12).\n\n**J2 Pin 2 is NFAULT.**\nU1.NFAULT -> J3.2.\nAlso U1.NFAULT -> J2.1 -> J2.2 -> U2.IND (Pin 11).\n\n**J17 Pin 3 is NFAULT_C.**\nU2.OUTD (Pin 6) -> J17.3.\n\n**J17 Pin 7 is USB2ANY_TX_3.3.**\nJ17.7 -> U2.INB (Pin 4).\n\n**J17 Pin 8 is USB2ANY_RX_3.3.**\nU2.OUTC (Pin 5) -> J17.8.\n\n**J18:**\n`CVDD` -> J18.1 -> J18.2 -> `CVDD_CO`.\n\n**J21:**\nU2.OUTB (Pin 13) -> `RX_CO` -> J21.1 -> J21.2 -> `RX`.\n\n**Conflict Check:**\n`RX` is driven by J21 (from U2) AND J1 (from J3).\nThis is a wired-OR or selection. The jumpers select the source.\nSo `net.RX` connects to U1.RX, J21.2, and J1.2.\n\n**Let\'s do it.**\n\n```tsx\nimport { BQ79616PAPR } from "./lib/BQ79616PAPR"\nimport { ISO7342FCQDWRQ1 } from "./lib/ISO7342FCQDWRQ1"\nimport { MMBT3904LT1G } from "./lib/MMBT3904LT1G"\nimport { A_150060GS75000 } from "./lib/A_150060GS75000"\nimport { BZX84C24 } from "./lib/BZX84C24"\nimport { NCP18XH103F03RB } from "./lib/NCP18XH103F03RB"\n\nexport default () => {\n  return (\n    <board width="150mm" height="100mm">\n      {/* Nets */}\n      <net name="PWR" />\n      <net name="GND" />\n      <net name="AVDD" />\n      <net name="CVDD" />\n      <net name="DVDD" />\n      <net name="TSREF" />\n      <net name="LDOIN" />\n      <net name="NEG5V" />\n      <net name="NPNB" />\n      <net name="REFHP" />\n      <net name="U1_BAT" />\n      \n      {/* Comms Nets */}\n      <net name="TX" />\n      <net name="RX" />\n      <net name="NFAULT" />\n      <net name="USB2ANY_3.3V" />\n      <net name="GND_ISO" />\n      <net name="CVDD_CO" />\n      <net name="RX_CO" />\n      <net name="NF_J" />\n      <net name="USB2ANY_TX_3.3" />\n      <net name="USB2ANY_RX_3.3" />\n      <net name="NFAULT_C" />\n      <net name="RX_C" />\n      <net name="RX_C_R" />\n      \n      {/* NPN Nets */}\n      <net name="NPN_R4_R3" />\n      <net name="NPN_C" />\n\n      {/* Main IC */}\n      <BQ79616PAPR name="U1" />\n\n      {/* U1 Power Connections */}\n      <trace from=".U1 > .AVSS" to="net.GND" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .CVSS" to="net.GND" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .DVSS" to="net.GND" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .EP" to="net.GND" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .REFHM" to="net.GND" />\n\n      <trace from=".U1 > .AVDD" to="net.AVDD" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .CVDD" to="net.CVDD" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .DVDD" to="net.DVDD" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .TSREF" to="net.TSREF" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .LDOIN" to="net.LDOIN" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .NEG5V" to="net.NEG5V" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .BBP1" to="net.NPNB" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .REFHP" to="net.REFHP" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .BAT" to="net.U1_BAT" />\n      \n      {/* U1 Comms Connections */}\n      <trace from=".U1 > .TX" to="net.TX" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .RX" to="net.RX" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .NFAULT" to="net.NFAULT" />\n\n      {/* BAT Filter */}\n      <resistor name="R5" resistance="30" footprint="0603" />\n      <capacitor name="C5" capacitance="10nF" footprint="0402" />\n      <trace from="net.PWR" to=".R5 > .pin1" />\n      <trace from=".R5 > .pin2" to="net.U1_BAT" />\n      <trace from=".C5 > .pin1" to="net.U1_BAT" />\n      <trace from=".C5 > .pin2" to="net.GND" />\n\n      {/* Decoupling Capacitors */}\n      <capacitor name="C6" capacitance="1uF" footprint="0603" />\n      <trace from=".C6 > .pin1" to="net.AVDD" />\n      <trace from=".C6 > .pin2" to="net.GND" />\n\n      <capacitor name="C9" capacitance="1uF" footprint="0603" />\n      <trace from=".