onent names.\nI will check if there are actual files for these components.\n`ls -F /home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/resources`\nIf not found, I will assume they are abstract imports. I will use a generic import path like `"./components"` or just assume they are globally available if that\'s a `tscircuit` feature (it\'s not usually).\nLet\'s try to find where these components might be defined.\nI\'ll search for `.tsx` files in the repo.\n\n**Let\'s check for component files.**\n`find . -name "*.tsx"`\n\nIf I can\'t find them, I will define them as "dummy" imports or just use the names. The prompt says "paths are managed by VHL; use relative imports". This implies I should know the path.\nMaybe I should look at `ana/resources/component_pin_mapping.md` again? No paths there.\nI\'ll assume they are in `../components` relative to the output file, or similar.\nActually, I will just use the component names as imports from a hypothetical `./lib` to satisfy the syntax, or check if I can find them.\n\nLet\'s do a quick search.\n`find /home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary -name "*.tsx"`\n\nIf no files found, I will use:\n`import { BQ79616PAPR } from "./components/BQ79616PAPR"`\netc.\n\n**Let\'s start building.**\n\n**Iteration 1: Setup and Main IC**\n*   Define Board\n*   Define Nets\n*   Instantiate U1\n*   Connect U1 Power/GND pins to nets.\n\n**Nets:**\n*   `PWR` (High Voltage Battery)\n*   `GND` (System Ground)\n*   `AVDD`, `CVDD`, `DVDD` (Internal Regulators)\n*   `TSREF` (Thermistor Ref)\n*   `LDOIN` (LDO Input)\n*   `NEG5V`\n*   `NPNB` (Base Drive)\n*   `REFHP`, `REFHM`\n\n**U1 Connections (Pass 1):**\n*   Pin 1 (BAT) -> `PWR` (via filter, but for now just net association or direct if filter is close) -> Actually SCUD says "R5 (30.0Ω), C5 (10nF) on BAT pin". I should add these.\n*   Pin 38 (AVDD) -> `AVDD`\n*   Pin 45 (CVDD) -> `CVDD`\n*   Pin 49 (DVDD) -> `DVDD`\n*   Pin 39, 46, 50 (AVSS, CVSS, DVSS) -> `GND`\n*   Pin 65 (EP) -> `GND`\n*   Pin 36 (REFHM) -> `GND`\n*   Pin 37 (REFHP) -> `REFHP` net\n*   Pin 44 (NEG5V) -> `NEG5V` net\n*   Pin 47 (LDOIN) -> `LDOIN` net\n*   Pin 48 (BBP1/NPNB) -> `NPNB` net\n*   Pin 51 (TSREF) -> `TSREF` net\n\nI will start with this.\n\n**Wait, I need to handle the imports correctly.**\nI\'ll assume the components are in a `components` folder.\n`import { BQ79616PAPR } from "./components/BQ79616PAPR"`\n`import { ISO7342FCQDWRQ1 } from "./components/ISO7342FCQDWRQ1"`\n`import { MMBT3904LT1G } from "./components/MMBT3904LT1G"`\n`import { A_150060GS75000 } from "./components/A_150060GS75000"`\n`import { BZX84C24 } from "./components/BZX84C24"`\n`import { NCP18XH103F03RB } from "./components/NCP18XH103F03RB"`\n\nI will create the file `ana/output/bq79616_eval_board.tsx`.\n\n**Pass 1 Content:**\n*   Imports\n*   Board\n*   Nets\n*   U1\n*   U1 Decoupling (C6, C9, C7, C8, C3, C59, C2)\n*   U1 BAT Filter (R5, C5)\n\n**Decoupling details from SCUD:**\n*   AVDD (Pin 38): C6 (1uF)\n*   CVDD (Pin 45): C9 (1uF)\n*   DVDD (Pin 49): C7 (4.7uF), C8 (1uF) -> SCUD says "C7 (4.7uF), C8 (1uF)". Usually one per pin or shared. I\'ll put both on DVDD net near pin 49.\n*   LDOIN (Pin 47): C59 (0.1uF)\n*   NEG5V (Pin 44): C3 (0.1uF)\n*   TSREF (Pin 51): C2 (1uF)\n*   REFHP (Pin 37): Not explicitly listed in "Internal Regulators" list but usually needs a cap. SCUD says "TP7 (REFHP)". I\'ll check if there\'s a cap. SCUD doesn\'t list one for REFHP in the "Internal Regulators" bullet. I\'ll leave it off unless I see it in the image or later.\n    *   Wait, looking at "Internal Regulators" list again: "AVDD/CVDD/DVDD: Decoupled by C6, C9, C7, C8".\n    *   "LDOIN: C59".\n    *   "NEG5V: C3".\n    *   "TSREF: C2".\n    *   "Isolator Power: C57, C58".\n    *   Nothing for REFHP.\n\n**BAT Filter:**\n*   `PWR` net -> R5 (30R) -> `U1_BAT` net -> U1 Pin 1.\n*   `U1_BAT` net -> C5 (10nF) -> `GND`.\n\nLet\'s write this.'}], 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_d40e1a20009