19.\n*   Thermistors: RT1..RT8.\n*   J4 (2x8 Header):\n    *   Connects `GPIOx` (U1) to `GPIOx_R` (Divider).\n    *   Pinout: SCUD says "J4 allows connecting the BMS IC\'s GPIOx pins... to the measurement points."\n    *   Usually Pin 1-2, 3-4, etc.\n    *   Let\'s assume Pin 1=GPIO1, Pin 2=GPIO1_Meas. Or Pin 1=Meas, Pin 2=GPIO.\n    *   SCUD: "Channel 1... GPIO1_C connects to J4 Pin 2. Thus, the BMS pin GPIO1 measures..."\n    *   So J4 Pin 2 is `GPIO1_C`. J4 Pin 1 is likely `GPIO1` (U1 Pin 61).\n    *   Wait, "GPIO1 connects directly to GPIOx_R when the jumper is placed."\n    *   For Channel 1: `GPIO1_R` -> Filter -> `GPIO1_C` -> J4.2 -> Jumper -> J4.1 -> `GPIO1`.\n    *   For Channels 2-8: `GPIOx_R` -> J4.even -> Jumper -> J4.odd -> `GPIOx`.\n    *   I\'ll assume J4 Odd pins = U1 GPIOs, J4 Even pins = Divider points.\n    *   Mapping:\n        *   GPIO1: J4.1 - J4.2 (Signal `GPIO1_C`)\n        *   GPIO2: J4.3 - J4.4 (Signal `GPIO2_R`)\n        *   ...\n        *   GPIO8: J4.15 - J4.16 (Signal `GPIO8_R`)\n\n**GPIO1 Filter:**\n*   `GPIO1_R` -> R128 (1k) -> `GPIO1_C`.\n*   `GPIO1_R` -> C60 (1uF) -> `GND`.\n*   `GPIO1_R` -> D3 (Cathode) -> `GND`? SCUD says "D3: 24V Dual Zener/TVS". Usually Cathode to Signal, Anode to GND. Or Bidirectional.\n*   Mapping for `BZX84C24`: pin1=Anode, pin2=pin2, pin3=Cathode.\n*   Dual Zener usually has common anode or cathode. SOT-23.\n*   If it\'s a dual series zener (bidirectional), it might be Pin 1 and 2 to lines, Pin 3 to GND? Or Pin 3 is common.\n*   SCUD says "D3: 24V Dual Zener/TVS Diode".\n*   I\'ll check `subckt_gpios.png` if I can.\n*   If not, I\'ll assume standard protection: Signal -> D3 -> GND.\n*   I\'ll use `BZX84C24` pin 1 and 3? Or just 1 and 2?\n*   Let\'s assume Pin 3 (Cathode) to Signal, Pin 1 (Anode) to GND.\n\n**Aux Measurement:**\n*   `BBP` (U1-64) and `BBN` (U1-63).\n*   Path 2 (Active): `SRP_S` -> `BBP`, `SRN_S` -> `BBN`.\n*   Path 1 (DNP): `BBP_CELL` -> R9 -> `BBP`. `BBN_CELL` -> R12 -> `BBN`.\n*   I\'ll define nets `SRP_S`, `SRN_S`, `BBP_CELL`, `BBN_CELL`.\n*   Connect `SRP_S` to `BBP`.\n*   Connect `SRN_S` to `BBN`.\n*   Add R9, R12, C10 (DNP/Active?). SCUD says Path 1 is DNP.\n*   "R9, R12 (402Ω)... Currently DNP."\n*   "C10 (0.47uF)..."\n*   I\'ll add them but maybe not connect them to the main nets if they are DNP? No, I should wire them as if the PCB exists.\n*   So: `BBP_CELL` -> R9 -> `BBP`. `BBN_CELL` -> R12 -> `BBN`.\n*   C10 between `BBP` and `BBN`? Or before resistors? "Differential RC filter formed by R9/R12 and C10". Usually C is after R. So C10 between `BBP` and `BBN`.\n*   Path 2: "Directly wired to BBP/BBN".\n*   So `SRP_S` -> `BBP`. `SRN_S` -> `BBN`.\n\n**LED:**\n*   `PWR` -> R121 (1k) -> J6.1 -> J6.2 -> D1 (Anode) -> D1 (Cathode) -> `GND`.\n*   Wait, SCUD says "Green LED D1 with R121 (1.0k) and Jumper J6".\n*   Usually LED is on low voltage side? No, "Power Indicator".\n*   If it\'s on `PWR` (High Voltage), 1k is too small for HV (e.g. 48V).\n*   Maybe it\'s on `LDOIN` or `CVDD`?\n*   SCUD says "Indicator: Green LED D1...". Doesn\'t explicitly say which rail.\n*   But "NPN Supply... Input Path: PWR...".\n*   Let\'s check `subckt_test_points.png` or `subckt_pow_supply.png`.\n*   Actually, if it\'s a "High-cell-count BMS", PWR is HV.\n*   Maybe it\'s on `CVDD` (5V) or `DVDD`?\n*   I\'ll assume `CVDD` or `LDOIN`.\n*   Let\'s look at the text again. "Indicator: Green LED D1...".\n*   I\'ll check `subckt_pow_supply.png` again.\n\nI\'ll delete the file and start the full build including Pass 3.\n\n**Full Build Plan:**\n1.  Imports.\n2.  Board.\n3.  Nets (Power, Comms, Aux, GPIOs).\n4.  U1 Instantiation & Power/Decoupling.\n5.  NPN Supply.\n6.  Isolator U2 & Comms Connectors.\n7.  Cell Inputs (Direct & Config Resistors).\n8.  Thermistors & GPIO Interface.\n9.  Aux Inputs.\n10. LED.\n\n**LED Rail:** I\'ll guess `CVDD` (5V) or `LDOIN`. 1k resistor on 5V gives 3mA (dim) or 5mA. On 48V it would burn. So it must be a low voltage rail. `CVDD` is a good candidate.\n\n**Cell Inputs:**\nI need to add `VC0`..`VC16` and `CB0`..`CB16` nets.\nAnd connect them to U1.\nAnd add the config resistors.\n\n**Thermistors:**\nI need to add 8x `resistor` (10k), 8x `NCP18XH103F03RB`.\nAnd J5.\nAnd J4.\nAnd the GPIO1 filter.\n\n**Let\'s go.**\n\nI\'ll delete the file first.'}], 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_1693be3653db49d0966c8fb1ba83', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'terminal', 'arguments': '{"security_risk": "LOW", "command": "rm ana/output/bq79616_eval_board.tsx"}'}}]}, {'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': '\x1b[?2004l\x1b[?2004h\n[The command completed with exit code 0.]\n[Current working directory: /home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary]\n[Python interpreter: /home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/.venv/bin/python]\n[Command finished with exit code 0]'}], 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_1693be3653db49d0966c8fb1ba83', 'name': 'terminal'}, {'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'thought:Now I will create the final file. I will try to be as complete as possible.\n\n**One detail on Thermistors:**\n"RT1-RT8: NCP18XH103F03RB".\n"Pullup Resistors (10.0k): R7, R8, R11, R14, R15, R16, R18, R19."\nI need to map which R goes to which RT.\nSCUD doesn\'t explicitly pair them (e.g. "R7 with RT1").\nI\'ll assume sequential: R7-RT1, R8-RT2, R11-RT3, R14-RT4, R15-RT5, R16-RT6, R18-RT7, R19-RT8.\nOr I can just name them `R_PU1`..`R_PU8` if I don\'t want to guess the designators, but I should try to use the SCUD designators.\nThe list is: R7, R8, R11, R14, R15, R16, R18, R19. (8 resistors).\nThermistors: RT1..RT8.\nI\'ll pair them in order.\n\n**GPIO Mapping:**\nGPIO1 -> RT1 (via Filter)\nGPIO2 -> RT2\n...\nGPIO8 -> RT8.\n\n**Aux Inputs:**\n`SRP_S`, `SRN_S` nets.\n`BBP_CELL`, `BBN_CELL` nets.\nR9, R12, C10.\nR17 (DNP).\n\n**LED:**\nI\'ll put it on `CVDD`.\n\n**Cell Inputs:**\nI\'ll loop or just write them out. 16 channels is a lot to write manually but I must do it.\n\n**Let\'s write the code.**\n\n```tsx\nimport { BQ79616PAPR } from "./lib/BQ79616PAPR"\nimport { ISO7342FCQDWRQ1 } from "./lib/ISO7342FCQDWRQ1"\nimport { MMBT3904LT1G } from "./lib/MMBT3904LT1G"\nimport { A_150060GS75000 } from "./lib/A_150060GS75000"\nimport { BZX84C24 } from "./lib/BZX84C24"\nimport { NCP18XH103F03RB } from "./lib/NCP18XH103F03RB"\n\nexport default () => {\n  return (\n    <board width="150mm" height="100mm">\n      {/* --------------------------------------------------------- */}\n      {/* NETS */}\n      {/* --------------------------------------------------------- */}\n      <net name="PWR" />\n      <net name="GND" />\n      <net name="AVDD" />\n      <net name="CVDD" />\n      <net name="DVDD" />\n      <net name="TSREF" />\n      <net name="LDOIN" />\n      <net name="NEG5V" />\n      <net name="NPNB" />\n      <net name="REFHP" />\n      <net name="U1_BAT" />\n      \n      {/* Comms */}\n      <net name="TX" />\n      <net name="RX" />\n      <net name="NFAULT" />\n      <net name="USB2ANY_3.3V" />\n      <net name="GND_ISO" />\n      <net name="CVDD_CO" />\n      <net name="RX_CO" />\n      <net name="NF_J" />\n      <net name="USB2ANY_TX_3.3" />\n      <net name="USB2ANY_RX_3.3" />\n      <net name="NFAULT_C" />\n      <net name="RX_C" />\n      <net name="RX_C_R" />\n      \n      {/* NPN */}\n      <net name="NPN_R4_R3" />\n      <net name="NPN_C" />\n      \n      {/* Aux */}\n      <net name="SRP_S" />\n      <net name="SRN_S" />\n      <net name="BBP_CELL" />\n      <net name="BBN_CELL" />\n      <net name="BBP" />\n      <net name="BBN" />\n      \n      {/* Thermistors */}\n      <net name="PULLUP" />\n      <net name="GPIO1_R" />\n      <net name="GPIO1_C" />\n      <net name="GPIO2_R" />\n      <net name="GPIO3_R" />\n      <net name="GPIO4_R" />\n      <net name="GPIO5_R" />\n      <net name="GPIO6_R" />\n      <net name="GPIO7_R" />\n      <net name="GPIO8_R" />\n      \n      {/* Cell Inputs */}\n      <net name="VC0" /> <net name="VC1" /> <net name="VC2" /> <net name="VC3" />\n      <net name="VC4" /> <net name="VC5" /> <net name="VC6" /> <net name="VC7" />\n      <net name="VC8" /> <net name="VC9" /> <net name="VC10" /> <net name="VC11" />\n      <net name="VC12" /> <net name="VC13" /> <net name="VC14" /> <net name="VC15" /> <net name="VC16" />\n      \n      <net name="CB0" /> <net name="CB1" /> <net name="CB2" /> <net name="CB3" />\n      <net name="CB4" /> <net name="CB5" /> <net name="CB6" /> <net name="CB7" />\n      <net name="CB8" /> <net name="CB9" /> <net name="CB10" /> <net name="CB11" />\n      <net name="CB12" /> <net name="CB13" /> <net name="CB14" /> <net name="CB15" /> <net name="CB16" />\n\n      {/* --------------------------------------------------------- */}\n      {/* MAIN IC U1 */}\n      {/* --------------------------------------------------------- */}\n      <BQ79616PAPR name="U1" />\n\n      {/* Power & GND */}\n      <trace from=".U1 > .AVSS" to="net.GND" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .CVSS" to="net.GND" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .DVSS" to="net.GND" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .EP" to="net.GND" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .REFHM" to="net.GND" />\n\n      <trace from=".U1 > .AVDD" to="net.AVDD" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .CVDD" to="net.CVDD" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .DVDD" to="net.DVDD" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .TSREF" to="net.TSREF" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .LDOIN" to="net.LDOIN" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .NEG5V" to="net.NEG5V" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .BBP1" to="net.NPNB" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .REFHP" to="net.REFHP" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .BAT" to="net.U1_BAT" />\n      \n      {/* Comms */}\n      <trace from=".U1 > .TX" to="net.TX" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .RX" to="net.RX" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .NFAULT" to="net.NFAULT" />\n      \n      {/* Aux */}\n      <trace from=".U1 > .BBP2" to="net.BBP" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .BBN" to="net.BBN" />\n      \n      {/* GPIOs */}\n      <trace from=".U1 > .GPIO1" to=".J4 > .pin1" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .GPIO2" to=".J4 > .pin3" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .GPIO3" to=".J4 > .pin5" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .GPIO4" to=".J4 > .pin7" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .GPIO5" to=".J4 > .pin9" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .GPIO6" to=".J4 > .pin11" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .GPIO7" to=".J4 > .pin13" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .GPIO8" to=".J4 > .pin15" />\n      \n      {/* Cell Inputs */}\n      <trace from=".U1 > .VC0" to="net.VC0" /> <trace from=".U1 > .CB0" to="net.CB0" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .VC1" to="net.VC1" /> <trace from=".U1 > .CB1" to="net.CB1" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .VC2" to="net.VC2" /> <trace from=".U1 > .CB2" to="net.CB2" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .VC3" to="net.VC3" /> <trace from=".U1 > .CB3" to="net.CB3" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .VC4" to="net.VC4" /> <trace from=".U1 > .CB4" to="net.CB4" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .VC5" to="net.VC5" /> <trace from=".U1 > .CB5" to="net.CB5" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .VC6" to="net.VC6" /> <trace from=".U1 > .CB6" to="net.CB6" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .VC7" to="net.VC7" /> <trace from=".U1 > .CB7" to="net.CB7" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .VC8" to="net.VC8" /> <trace from=".U1 > .CB8" to="net.CB8" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .VC9" to="net.VC9" /> <trace from=".U1 > .CB9" to="net.CB9" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .VC10" to="net.VC10" /> <trace from=".U1 > .CB10" to="net.CB10" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .VC11" to="net.VC11" /> <trace from=".U1 > .CB11" to="net.CB11" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .VC12" to="net.VC12" /> <trace from=".U1 > .CB12" to="net.CB12" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .VC13" to="net.VC13" /> <trace from=".U1 > .CB13" to="net.CB13" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .VC14" to="net.VC14" /> <trace from=".U1 > .CB14" to="net.CB14" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .VC15" to="net.VC15" /> <trace from=".U1 > .CB15" to="net.CB15" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .VC16" to="net.VC16" /> <trace from=".U1 > .CB16" to="net.CB16" />\n\n      {/* --------------------------------------------------------- */}\n      {/* POWER SUPPLY & DECOUPLING */}\n      {/* --------------------------------------------------------- */}\n      \n      {/* BAT Filter */}\n      <resistor name="R5" resistance="30" footprint="0603" />\n      <capacitor name="C5" capacitance="10nF" footprint="0402" />\n      <trace from="net.PWR" to=".R5 > .pin1" />\n      <trace from=".R5 > .pin2" to="net.U1_BAT" />\n      <trace from=".C5 > .pin1" to="net.U1_BAT" />\n      <trace from=".C5 > .pin2" to="net.GND" />\n\n      {/* Decoupling */}\n      <capacitor name="C6" capacitance="1uF" footprint="0603" />\n      <trace from=".C6 > .pin1" to="net.AVDD" /> <trace from=".C6 > .pin2" to="net.GND" />\n\n      <capacitor name="C9" capacitance="1uF" footprint="0603" />\n      <trace from=".C9 > .pin1" to="net.CVDD" /> <trace from=".C9 > .pin2" to="net.GND" />\n\n      <capacitor name="C7" capacitance="4.7uF" footprint="0805" />\n      <capacitor name="C8" capacitance="1uF" footprint="0603" />\n      <trace from=".C7 > .pin1" to="net.DVDD" /> <trace from=".C7 > .pin2" to="net.GND" />\n      <trace from=".C8 > .pin1" to="net.DVDD" /> <trace from=".C8 > .pin2" to="net.GND" />\n\n      <capacitor name="C59" capacitance="0.1uF" footprint="0402" />\n      <trace from=".C59 > .pin1" to="net.LDOIN" /> <trace from=".C59 > .pin2" to="net.GND" />\n\n      <capacitor name="C3" capacitance="0.1uF" footprint="0402" />\n      <trace from=".C3 > .pin1" to="net.NEG5V" /> <trace from=".C3 > .pin2" to="net.GND" />\n\n      <capacitor name="C2" capacitance="1uF" footprint="0603" />\n      <trace from=".C2 > .pin1" to="net.TSREF" /> <trace from=".C2 > .pin2" to="net.GND" />\n      \n      {/* NPN Supply */}\n      <resistor name="R4" resistance="200" footprint="0603" />\n      <resistor name="R3" resistance="100" footprint="0603" />\n      <capacitor name="C1" capacitance="0.22uF" footprint="0603" />\n      <MMBT3904LT1G name="Q1" />\n      \n      <trace from="net.PWR" to=".R4 > .pin1" />\n   